From 2c5853529e24ad07cfbacfebdf20ffcdec14efd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work8_fin_tc <adbtrr_work8_fin_tc@local>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 06:21:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] os/kernel/clock: Add ASSERT hitting test case for
 clock_systimespec

clock_systimespec() turns the wall clock time reported by a high
resolution RTC into the time since power up by subtracting g_basetime,
the wall clock time the system booted at. A base time which sits in the
future of the RTC would make that difference negative, so the subtraction
is guarded by DEBUGASSERT(ts->tv_sec >= g_basetime.tv_sec).

Add a negative test case which moves g_basetime one year ahead of the
RTC and then reads the time since power up, which is the inconsistent
state the assertion is there to catch. g_basetime is restored on the
path taken when the assertion is compiled out.

 - os/drivers/os_api_test/kernel/test_assert_clock.c : kernel side
   helper reached through the TESTIOC_ASSERT_CLOCK ioctl.
 - apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/tc_assert_clock.c : user side
   test case. A return from the ioctl is reported as a test case failure.

Controlled by CONFIG_TC_KERNEL_ASSERT_CLOCK, default n, depends on
CONFIG_RTC_HIRES and CONFIG_DEBUG. The helper reports -EAGAIN when the
RTC is not running yet. It crashes the board by design and must be
enabled alone.
